{\b\fs40 Film 19: Can you get up off the floor without your hands?}\par\par
Posts 2026-12-01. Read each line twice, in your own voice: savage, direct, funny. Leave three seconds of silence after each take. One audio file for the whole film, into folder 3 Your recordings.\par\par
{\b Line 1}\par You treat the floor like lava now: down is easy, but up needs a hand, a knee, and a small prayer to the sofa. You have not lost a party trick. You have lost a basic move.\par\par
{\b Line 2}\par Your body was built to sit on the floor and stand back up in one piece, using strength, balance and flexibility together.\par\par
{\b Line 3}\par Researchers scored exactly that move in two thousand and two adults who sat on the floor and rose again.\par\par
{\b Line 4}\par Every hand or knee cost a point, and low scores were linked to higher death rates afterwards.\par\par
{\b Line 5}\par Each extra point was linked to a twenty one percent improvement in survival.\par\par
{\b Line 6}\par So win the points back beside a sturdy chair: its seat first, then one hand, then a fingertip, then nothing.\par\par
{\b Line 7}\par Train the parts twice a week: chair stands, calf raises, and slow trips down to the floor and back.\par\par
{\b Line 8}\par Plain warning: if you have fallen, hurt your head, back, neck or hip, or you cannot get up, call for emergency help and keep warm while you wait. If you have not exercised for a while, talk to your doctor first.\par\par
{\b Line 9}\par Let's get you back to factory settings.\par\par
